Subject: [LOCAL PROPOSAL] Require whole usernames during TRAMP expansion validation
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (changes to GNU Emacs)

Apply to GNU Emacs 31.1 after Nixpkgs' CVE-2026-108976 patch.
This is source-only validation hardening, not an applied Nixi package change.
Whole-string matching at the domain split preserves invalid input for rejection;
whole-string revalidation checks the complete expanded/default username.
Host grammar and existing connection-local percent policy are unchanged.
No CVE assignment, upstream acceptance or consumer exploitability is claimed.

--- a/lisp/net/tramp.el
+++ b/lisp/net/tramp.el
@@ -1855,7 +1855,8 @@
 	(when user
 	  (while (string-match (rx bos "$" (group (+ (any "_" alnum))) eos) user)
 	    (setq user (getenv (match-string 1 user))))
-	  (when (string-match tramp-user-with-domain-regexp user)
+	  (when (string-match
+		 (rx bos (regexp tramp-user-with-domain-regexp) eos) user)
 	    (setq domain (match-string 2 user)
 		  user (match-string 1 user))))
 
@@ -1910,7 +1911,8 @@
 	      ;; environment variables, or contain a literal
 	      ;; environment variable.
 	      (unless (tramp-string-empty-or-nil-p user)
-		(when (or (not (string-match-p tramp-user-regexp user))
+		(when (or (not (string-match-p
+			   (rx bos (regexp tramp-user-regexp) eos) user))
 			  (string-match-p
 			   (rx "$") (tramp-file-name-user-domain v))
 			  (and (not allow-double-percent)
